<title>FRANCE: Technip wins N. Sea, Arab Emirates orders.</title>
<headline>Technip wins N. Sea, Arab Emirates orders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French engineering group Technip said on Friday it was part of a consortium which won a contract for a TPG 500 oil platform in the Elgin and Franklin fields in the British sector of the North Sea.</p>
<p>Technip estimated the total value of the contract at some 3.56 billion francs and put its share at a little over one billion francs.</p>
<p>Technip also said it signed a contract worth some 900 million francs with a United Arab Emirates company, Ras Al Khimah Cement Co, for a turn-key cement plant in the Ras Al Khimah Emirate.</p>
</text>
